  "name": "ALLERGY INDIVIDUAL DRUG AMOXYCILLIN ANTIBIOTIC",
  "code": "2653",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"82\">Amoxycillin</strong> is a widely used <strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"126\">beta-lactam antibiotic</strong>. Allergic reactions to amoxycillin are among the most common drug allergies, particularly in children and adults with penicillin sensitivity. The <strong data-start=\"273\" data-end=\"301\">Amoxycillin allergy test</strong> aims to determine if a person is <strong data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"353\">hypersensitive</strong> to this antibiotic.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Reactive)</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>sensitization to amoxycillin</strong>. The individual is likely allergic and should avoid amoxycillin and possibly other penicillins.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative (Non-Reactive)</strong></td>\n<td>No evidence of sensitization at the time of testing. However, a <strong>negative test does not completely rule out</strong> an allergy, especially if there's a strong clinical history.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equivocal/Borderline</strong></td>\n<td>Unclear result; <strong>repeat testing</strong> or <strong>drug challenge</strong> under medical supervision may be necessary.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
